THE TEST IS BY POINTER, NEVER BY TEXT, and that is the whole design of this
file. A wrapper and the thing it wraps READ THE SAME -- both answer with the
caller's value, because the auto-unwrap makes the wrapper transparent. Text
cannot tell them apart and never could. showBody is the only way to ask.

    LEGACY  the argument is a CARRIER: its groupBody DIFFERS from the caller's
    FLIPPED the argument IS the caller's storage: groupBody IDENTICAL

⚠ COMPARE THE groupBody, NOT THE node. The node is expected to differ in both
arms -- the argument slot is a persistent node on the action, re-pointed per
call, and it stays one under bind-by-body. It is the BODY that is adopted, and
the body is also the thing that was already stable: filmed 2026-08-30, two calls
passing the same source field arrive as DIFFERENT NODES OVER ONE BODY. Binding
by body binds to what was already invariant, which is why this is the honest
comparison rather than a convenient one.

